    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you. Could you please tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, Dr. Smith, I came in because... see, I know the people over at my apartment are watching my comings and goings. They're always slipping these notes about me down to the main office. Now, everybody keeps telling me it's just regular notices taped on the doors, but I know what it really is. \n\nIt's funny though, doors... my uncle used to make doors. Well, frames mostly, out of this heavy oak. He had a woodshop out back of his place. Smelled like sawdust and motor oil all the time in there. I used to sit out there when I was a kid and just watch him sand the wood down until it was smooth as glass. He had this old hound dog too, Buster, who would just sleep right in the pile of shavings and sneeze when the dust got too thick. We used to feed him scraps from the table... \n\nBut anyway, yeah, the people at the building are definitely keeping tabs on me with those notes.",
