    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from these concerns about your neighbors, have you been feeling unusually depressed, hopeless, or perhaps the complete opposite—like you have an excessive amount of energy or need very little sleep?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S024",
      "patient_response": "Well, I definitely don't have any extra energy, I can tell you that. It's mostly the other way around. Most mornings I wake up with this heavy, hollow feeling... like the day already went bad before I even get my feet on the floor. \n\nAnd that floor gets awful cold, too. The linoleum in my kitchen is starting to peel up at the edges. It's that old yellow kind with the little square patterns, you know? My ma used to have the exact same flooring in our house back when I was growing up. She'd be down there on her knees scrubbing it with a toothbrush and some pine cleaner every single Sunday. Smelled so strong it made your eyes water, but she swore it kept the ants away. We had a terrible ant problem one summer. They got into the sugar bowl, and I remember pouring sugar on my cornflakes and the whole bowl was just moving... had to throw the whole box of cereal out in the yard for the birds. The blue jays really liked it. \n\nBut anyway... what were you asking? Oh, about energy. Yeah, no, just that heavy feeling when I wake up mostly.",
