    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have there been times in the past, or is it happening now, where you've had these strong beliefs about your neighbors while also feeling this deep, hollow depression at the same time?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Well, yeah... it's exactly like that. When I'm stuck down in that hollow place, you know, when I'm barely eating anything and I just let the phone ring and ring... that's when I'm the most sure about the apartment people tracking me. That's when I know they're talking to the main office about me. \n\nPhones are funny things now, aren't they? Used to be you had one phone in the house, hung on the kitchen wall with a cord that could stretch all the way into the living room. Ours was this ugly avocado green color. My sister used to stretch that cord so far it would get all tangled up like a spring that lost its bounce. She'd sit on the floor for hours talking to her boyfriend, twisting that cord around her finger until the tip turned purple. My dad would get so mad because he was expecting a call from the union hall about a job down at the plant. He worked at the bottling plant for twenty years... came home smelling like stale soda syrup every night. \n\nBut yeah, when I'm feeling real low like that, that's when I know for a fact they're keeping tabs on me and slipping those notes around.",
