    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever experienced a period of time, lasting at least several days, where you felt unusually 'high,' irritable, or energized, even if you don't feel that way right now?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I... I've never felt like that. Never had that kind of energy where I'm all wired up or anything. I'm usually just tired. \n\nTired... you know, I used to get so tired when I worked at the hardware store. Not the big chain ones they have now with the bright orange signs, but a little local place on Main Street. Mr. Henderson owned it. He had this old brass cash register that went *ding* real loud every time you opened the drawer. We sold everything in there, from loose nails you had to weigh on a scale to these little glass fuses for old houses. Nobody uses those fuses anymore. Now it's all breaker boxes. My buddy Tom tried to wire his own breaker box once and ended up knocking out the power to his whole street for two days. The electric company was furious. They had these big yellow trucks with the bucket lifts on the back... \n\nBut, uh, no. I've never had a time where I felt high or energized like you're talking about. Just... just the heavy feeling.",
